NRC Report ID: <a href="http://www.nrc.uscg.mil/reports/rwservlet?standard_web+inc_seq=832026">832026</a><br/>Incident Time: 2007-04-11 19:15:00<br/>Nearest City: Kinston, NC<br/>Incident Type: STORAGE TANK<br/>Material: CHLOR-O-CLEAN (DETERGENT)<br/>Medium Affected: AIR<br/>Suspected Responsible Party: PROLOGISTICS<br/><b>Skytruth Analysis</b><br/>Reported Spill Volume: 570 gallons<br/>CALLER STATED A DRIVER WAS FILLING A STORAGE TANK FROM 275 GALLON TOTE THROUGH A PIPELINE SYSTEM.  THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF CHLORINE GAS WHICH CAUSED THE EVACUATION OF THE FACILITY.   CALLER STATED THE MATERIALS THAT WERE MIXED WERE DETERGENT AND THIS RESULTED IN A RELEASE OF CHLORINE GAS.  DETERGENT


///////PREVIOUSILY REPORTED ON INCIDENT NUMBER 831953///////////
CALLER IS REPORTING THAT A MIXTURE OF SODIUM HYPOCHLORITE AND ANOTHER CHEMICAL WERE BEING FILLED FROM A 750 GALLON TOTE INTO A CLEANING SOLUTION, WHEN A VAPOR OCCURRED DUE TO UNKNOWN CAUSES AND CAUSED AN EVACUATION OF THE BUILDING.  CALLER STATED THAT AT LEAST ONE EMPLOYEE AND A CONTRACTOR WERE REPORTED INJURED. THE ENTIRE BUILDING CONTAINING 150 EMPLOYEES AND CONTRACTORS WERE EVACUATED. STATE AND LOCAL AGENCIES ARE ON SITE.
